1
00:00:00,230 --> 00:00:02,240
A man looked at Aban ibn ‘Uthman

2
00:00:02,430 --> 00:00:04,570
and asked him a question that changed the story.

3
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:09,380
Aban ibn ‘Uthman (may Allah have mercy on him) used to narrate from his father ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)

4
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,960
that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said:

5
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:12,840
Whoever says:

6
00:00:13,270 --> 00:00:17,090
“In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm,

7
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:19,470
and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing” — three times,

8
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,860
no sudden affliction will strike him until morning.

9
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:24,960
Now Aban had been struck by paralysis.

10
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:28,080
The man who heard the hadith kept looking at him.

11
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,510
Aban said to him:

12
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:30,510
“Why are you staring?

13
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,810
The hadith is exactly as I told you,

14
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:36,490
but I did not say it on that day, so that Allah’s decree would take its course.”

15
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,320
(Narrated by Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi)

16
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:41,320
The morning and evening adhkar are a fortress from Allah,

17
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:45,090
but they do not prevent Allah’s decree when He wills to test His servant.

18
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:48,020
And it does not mean that whoever falls ill was negligent in dhikr.

19
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:49,560
So keep this dhikr,

20
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:52,150
and say it three times, morning and evening.

21
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:55,720
Share this story with someone you love, and follow the channel.

